			"notes": "first public beta of meshac, a native anticheat that runs inside a fabric server. players install nothing.\n\npick the jar for your server version (needs fabric api):\n\n- `meshac-0.1.0-mc26.1.jar` for 26.1.x (java 25)\n- `meshac-0.1.0-mc26.2.jar` for 26.2 (java 25)\n- `meshac-0.1.0-mc26.3.jar` for 26.3 (java 25)\n- `meshac-0.1.0-mc1.21.11.jar` for 1.21.11 (java 21)\n\n## what it catches\n\nmovement, combat, building, mining, interaction and elytra checks. caught in real-client tests: flight, speed above sprint-jump pace, step, spider, jesus, fast climb, no slow, timer, blink (0.75 s and up), air jump, high jump, elytra fly, reach, criticals, crystal aura, anchor aura, auto totem, nuker, packet mine, ghost hand, auto clicker, and more. the per-module tables are in docs/coverage.md and docs/COVERAGE-METEOR.md.\n\n## how it was tested\n\nthe last full sweep ran 138 hack cases with 57 legit controls on the final jar. no legit control was flagged. details in docs/FINAL-SWEEP.md.\n\n## what it doesn't catch, or only half catches\n\n- kill-aura is caught on some runs and not others. it's counter based, so a patient aimed one can slip through.\n- bow aimbot, explosion knockback tricks, blink shorter than about 0.4 s, and boosts above 45 blocks per second are not caught.\n- speed at or below sprint-jump pace looks like a fast legit player, so it isn't flagged.\n- some modules are untested, and a few client runs (auto fish, auto sign, mass tpa) are only proven with scripted bots.\n\n## versions\n\nmovement and combat checks were run on 26.1.2 and 26.2. the 1.21.11 and 26.3 jars load and boot, but have had no full client run yet.\n\n## chunkveil\n\nanti-xray and anti-esp are in the jar but off by default. they've only been tested with protocol bots, not a real client. with anti-xray on, players see about 2% fake ores. turn them on with `veilXray` and `veilEsp` in the config if you want to try them.\n\n## punishments\n\na flag puts the player back, then holds them, then kicks. repeat offenders get tempbans that grow (10 min, 1 hour, 6 hours, 36 hours, up to 7 days). permanent bans are off unless you turn them on.\n\nlicence: agpl-3.0."
